# The vendor file SHAPE without the vendor: a 50-byte file header, a 4-byte header before every record
# (skipped, not parsed), and 0x00 fill after the last record. All values invented.
#
# Reader rule this case pins: padding bytes (0x00/0xFF) are skipped BEFORE a record header is consumed, so a
# record header must not START with a fill byte — here it is "HW" + a 2-byte sequence number. (A header that
# began with 0x00 would be eaten as fill and the decode would slide off by one byte.)
#
# 50-byte file header: "SYNTH-CDR FILE HEADER v1" (24 bytes) + 26 spaces
53 59 4E 54 48 2D 43 44 52 20 46 49 4C 45 20 48 45 41 44 45 52 20 76 31
20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20
# record header (4 bytes: 'H' 'W' seq=1) + record 1: imsi="12345", duration=60, roaming=TRUE, cellId="AB", party.number="9999"
48 57 00 01
65 19  80 05 31 32 33 34 35  81 01 3C  82 01 FF  83 02 41 42  A4 06  80 04 39 39 39 39
# record header ('H' 'W' seq=2) + record 2: imsi="67890", duration=0, roaming=FALSE, cellId="CD", party absent
48 57 00 02
65 11  80 05 36 37 38 39 30  81 01 00  82 01 00  83 02 43 44
# trailing zero fill
00 00 00 00 00 00
